  "verbalization": "Dalteparin is associated with the Splicing factor, proline- and glutamine-rich, which is a target of two compounds: [(3aS,4S,6R,10S,11aR)-6-acetyloxy-6,10-dimethyl-3-methylidene-2,7-dioxo-3a,4,5,8,9,10,11,11a-octahydrocyclodeca[b]furan-4-yl] (Z)-2-methylbut-2-enoate and 13-Demethyldysidenin. Both of these compounds have a shared target of Jurkat, suggesting a potential mechanism where Dalteparin may interact with these splicing factors to influence Jurkat cell behavior. The evidence indicates a possible pathway where Dalteparin modulates the activity of splicing factors, which in turn affect Jurkat cells. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Dalteparin in targeting splicing factors that are critical for Jurkat cell function, potentially through a mechanism involving the regulation of gene expression.",
